# EXAMPLE ONLY. This file is a template. It holds no real values and no secrets,
# which is why it can sit in the public repository. The real file is `.env`,
# which you create yourself on your own machine. `.env` is listed in .gitignore,
# so it is never committed or pushed to GitHub.
#
# THE LOCAL DEMO NEEDS NONE OF THIS. `npm run setup` and `npm start -- --seed`
# work with no .env file, no wallet, no account and no API key.
#
# A root .env is read by hardhat.config.js and the scripts in scripts/. It
# matters only for Polygon Amoy (optional) and for the cost columns of the gas
# report. To make one:
#   cp .env.example .env      then uncomment and fill in only the lines you need
# Put real values in .env only, never in this file.
#
# Every variable below is commented out on purpose. A variable that is present
# but EMPTY (for example `AMOY_RPC_URL=`) still overrides the Hardhat keystore,
# and the Amoy commands then fail (an empty AMOY_RPC_URL stops Hardhat with
# "Invalid URL value"). Leave a line commented out rather than empty.
#
# Reference: "Deployment" (Polygon Amoy) and "Configuration" in README.md.
# The oracle and the web app do not read this file. Their settings, all
# optional, are listed in oracle/README.md and frontend/README.md.

# --- Polygon Amoy: endpoint and deployer wallet -------------------------------
# Recommended: keep these two in Hardhat's encrypted keystore, not in a file:
#   npx hardhat keystore set AMOY_RPC_URL
#   npx hardhat keystore set DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY
# If you use the keystore, leave both lines below commented out.

# Amoy JSON-RPC endpoint (chain id 80002). This public endpoint needs no API key.
# Do not use rpc-amoy.polygon.technology (shut down) or polygon-amoy.drpc.org
# (its free plan fails some requests and refuses event queries over 100 blocks).
# AMOY_RPC_URL=https://polygon-amoy-bor-rpc.publicnode.com

# SECRET. Private key of ONE testnet-only wallet funded with free faucet POL
# (at least 0.4 POL for a deployment and one demo run). This wallet deploys
# the registry and is the regulator in `npm run demo:amoy`. Never use a wallet
# that holds real funds.
# DEPLOYER_PRIVATE_KEY=

# --- Polygon Amoy: source verification (optional) -----------------------------
# SECRET. Only for `npm run verify:amoy`. A free API key from an etherscan.io
# account also covers PolygonScan. It can live in the keystore as well.
# ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=

# --- Polygon Amoy: multi-wallet path (optional) -------------------------------
# Not needed for `npm run demo:amoy`, which derives the other actors from the
# deployer wallet. These are wallet ADDRESSES (0x and 40 hex digits), never
# private keys. On the local chain they are ignored: the scripts always use the
# Hardhat test accounts there.

# Gives the regulator role to a wallet other than the deployer, at deploy time.
# Leave it unset for `npm run demo:amoy`.
# REGULATOR_ADDRESS=

# The organizations that `npm run roles:amoy` onboards.
# MANUFACTURER_ADDRESS=
# DISTRIBUTOR_ADDRESS=
# RETAILER_ADDRESS=
# ORACLE_ADDRESS=

# Overrides the registry address from deployments/amoy.json in `npm run roles:amoy`.
# REGISTRY_ADDRESS=

# --- Gas report: cost columns (optional) --------------------------------------
# `npm run gas:report` lists gas only. A gas price adds a cost column in POL;
# a POL price as well adds one in USD. Both are positive decimal numbers, and
# POL_USD is ignored without GAS_PRICE_GWEI. Take them from a dated source and
# quote the date. For a single run, the command line is simpler:
#   GAS_PRICE_GWEI=30 POL_USD=0.25 npm run gas:report      (example values)
# GAS_PRICE_GWEI=
# POL_USD=
